<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39333" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psīlōthrum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-trum</span></b> ), i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίλωθρον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An unguent for removing the hair and making the skin
				smooth</i>, <i>a depilatory</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 24,
				10, 47, § 79</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 9, 37, §
			58</span></i>; <i><span class="en">32, 9, 47,
				§ 135</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Contr. 3</span></i>, praef. 3; <i><span class="en">Mart. 6,
				93, 9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>called also</i>
			ampeloleuce, <i><span class="en">Plin. 23, 1, 16, § 21</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
